{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1475685-some-questions-about-trinity","id":1475685,"title":"Some questions about trinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-02T15:10:10-08:00","id":1475685,"title":"Some questions about trinity","content":"So quick question or two<br /> 1: Because you can make multiple actions with mixed actions can you bypass the limit of one stunt per type with a attack roll by doing multiple attack actions against a single target.<br /> <br /> 2 I think it's wierd that each Psi Order has 10s of thousands of members who are prions but only one Prometheus Chamber. Are there multiple prometheus chambers for each order but each one is linked to a single proxy level psion. Are the orders capable of cloning additional chambers, I know the Chia Banu had to regrow thiers from pieces, just some quick thoughts before going to the gym. Post more when I have the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T18:26:41-08:00","id":1475695,"title":"","content":"1: No. You can only buy Inflict Damage once and then you can buy the Critical Injury Stunt once. These are explicitly stated as being able to be bought once per target. But, when fighting a large group of minions, is the only real &quot;loophole&quot; to that as each Success past their Defense takes out one.<br /> 2: Nope. One Prometheus Chamber per order.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T08:24:31-08:00","id":1475734,"title":"","content":"The Psi orders tested people and recruited in secret for years before they were public, then it was even easier. Even if their Psi chambers are only churning out ~10 psions a day each which would assume that it would take about an hour to use, if it takes a ~5 mins with most of that being loading people in and out they could churn out a lot more, mostly limited by how many they could find that were compatible and willing.<br /> <br /> I don't know what the canonical time it takes to use a prometheous chamber is, but I would imagine it to be somewhere around 10 mins. Once the orders figured out the logistics of getting people identified, it wasn't really a limiting factor, which is why they are also able/willing to activate psions that will work for other others or Aeon for instance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T08:54:24-08:00","id":1475735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1475685-some-questions-about-trinity#post1475685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So quick question or two<br /> 2 I think it's wierd that each Psi Order has 10s of thousands of members who are prions but only one Prometheus Chamber. Are there multiple prometheus chambers for each order but each one is linked to a single proxy level psion. Are the orders capable of cloning additional chambers, I know the Chia Banu had to regrow thiers from pieces, just some quick thoughts before going to the gym. Post more when I have the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's math it out.<br /> <br /> The proxies were selected &quot;late in the year&quot; in 2104, so let's say that's November 1st for the sake of argument. The most recent date found in the TC\u00c6on core rulebook is July 12, 2123, so let's take that as our &quot;present.&quot; That's 6827 days.<br /> <br /> Page 133 of TC\u00c6on lists the populations of each of the psi orders, but let's just take the Legions as our worst case scenario, since they're the most populous order with 30,000 psions, roughly one-third of all psions. I'm also assuming all those Legionnaires are psychokinetics, and were all dunked in the same Prometheus Chamber, for the purposes of this example.<br /> <br /> That's about 4.4 psychokinetics triggered per day. Assuming the Legions keeps the tank running 24 hours a day, that's 5.45 hours available for dunking, tank resetting, and tank maintenance for each psion. That's plenty. Let's be generous with our assumptions and round that up to five psions per day. That's still 4.8 hours available for each one.<br /> <br /> And every other tank gets used less than that. ISRA manages less than one psion a day, on average. Nor\u00e7a runs almost three days between each dunking.<br /> <br /> The numbers we're given are perfectly doable in the time allotted without needing multiple Prometheus Chambers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}